Det. Holt
Det. Holt: Raymond Holt: Dr. Elena Mora from the University of Manitoba has been surveying along Ironjaw Creek. She says bat activity has roughly doubled late in the season — hotspots near the town limits and Loon Ridge Road.

Other oddities tied to that uptick: deer sightings have plummeted almost overnight; hunters say trails went dead. Squirrels have been burying caches together in places they usually don’t — biologically odd, Mora said. Campers fled after flashlights flickered during a large swarm; they reported a faint “beep‑beep‑beep” overhead. Fresh, high scratch marks showed up on the oak by the Olander Barn as well.

Quiet town, but those patterns feel out of the ordinary. Want me to pull Mora’s full notes or follow up on any of those specifics?

